---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About | Kreativ Sound"
  description="About Kreativ Sound, an independent sound-design project creating atmospheric presets, sample packs, browser tools, and dark cinematic textures."
  canonical="https://kreativsound.com/about/"
  activeNav="about"
>
  <section class="card page-main brand-page">
    <div class="brand-hero">
      <div class="brand-hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">Independent sound design built around mood, clarity, and usable texture.</h1>
        <p class="page-lead">Kreativ Sound is Andrei Olaru's independent sound-design project: ambient, experimental, and cinematic materials that help creators move quickly without sacrificing identity.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="brand-hero-panel">
        <p class="product-section-kicker">What this is</p>
        <h2>A focused catalog, not a trend machine</h2>
        <p>Each release is meant to give producers, editors, and sound designers a stronger starting point: darker tone, faster workflow, and fewer generic sounds.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="brand-process" aria-labelledby="brand-process-title">
      <div class="brand-process-intro">
        <p class="product-section-kicker">Made for the moment before the track takes shape</p>
        <h2 id="brand-process-title">A small palette with a clear point of view.</h2>
        <p>Every pack begins with a specific job: establish space, introduce movement, add pressure, or leave a mark at a transition. The aim is to make choosing and shaping sound feel faster, not more crowded.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="brand-process-steps">
        <li><strong>Define the role</strong><span>Choose a limited family of pads, drones, sequences, one-shots, or FX around one kind of musical tension.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Keep the character</strong><span>Build enough variation for a session while protecting the imperfect detail that makes a sound recognizable.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Use it in context</strong><span>Bring the same material into Olaru music and practical guides, then keep the catalog connected to real creative work.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <div class="brand-route-actions" aria-label="Explore Kreativ Sound">
      <a class="button primary" href="/sounds/">Browse the sound catalog <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/music/">Hear the Olaru project <i class="fa-solid fa-headphones" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/updates/#guides">Read practical guides <i class="fa-solid fa-book-open" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
    </div>

    <div class="brand-grid">
      <article class="product-panel product-panel-modern product-panel-accent">
        <p class="product-section-kicker">Catalog</p>
        <h2>What Kreativ Sound releases</h2>
        <p>Preset packs, sample collections, and free companion releases for music production, film edits, transitions, dark ambient work, and cinematic electronic sessions.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="product-panel product-panel-modern">
        <p class="product-section-kicker">Principle</p>
        <h2>Built for practical use</h2>
        <p>Every release keeps a clear sound identity, practical file formats, and textures that can go straight into a session.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="product-panel product-panel-modern">
        <p class="product-section-kicker">Context</p>
        <h2>Part of the KREATIV ecosystem</h2>
        <p>Kreativ Sound sits inside the wider <a href="https://madebykreativ.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">KREATIV</a> network of independent creative tools and assets, alongside design and publishing projects with the same direct, product-led mindset.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
